    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the numbers and the record supports them, so this is decided on the arithmetic.\n\nTo the driver: you did arrive and you did wait, but not for long enough. The GPS trace runs from 17:15:00 to 17:19:00 — 25 stationary fixes (0.0 kph) about 24 m from the Plaza Singapura pin, comfortably inside the 120 m arrival radius for a LARGE_VENUE pickup — so the arrival test in POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are met, and the trip record's RIDER_NO_SHOW code with no boarding event meets limb (d). Limb (c) is where it fails. The continuous hold inside the geofence is 240 seconds (17:15:00 to 17:19:00) against a 300-second minimum for a LARGE_VENUE pickup: a 60-second shortfall. The clock runs from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from your 17:15:20 'arrived' tap, but even on the tap clock (17:15:20 to the 17:19:00 cancellation) the wait is 220 seconds, 80 seconds short. Nothing rescues that: POL-NS-05 does not fire (you were stationary, ~24 m away, not over 300 m out and not at 15 kph), POL-NS-03 does not apply (you were inside the arrival radius, not outside it), and POL-NS-04 does not apply (no locating message from the rider). Under POL-NS-06 a dwell short of the minimum means the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied — the waiting period is what the fee buys. The one route to summing separate in-geofence intervals, limb (i), needs a present and populated traffic advisory, and EV-ADVIS-09103-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so there is nothing to sum; in any event the trace shows a single interval only.\n\nTo the rider: the refund does not depend on where you were. I note the rider track places your device about 519 m from the pin with no qualifying in-radius fixes; that would have defeated POL-NS-04, and it does not matter here, because POL-NS-06 turns on the driver's own fixes.\n\nThe amount is not in dispute. The fare breakdown's cancellation-fee line of SGD 8.00 is the GREATER of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee (SGD 8.00) — the vehicle tier produced it — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect, and the whole SGD 8.00 is refunded. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and POL-NS-06 displaces it here (the anti-farming check would not have tripped in any event — 1 no-show termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips).\n\nNothing escalates. No POL-NS-08 limb applies (arrival marker 20 seconds from the nearest fix, no trace gaps, all 3 chat messages present, the fee reconciles), and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires (no contradicting artifacts, no counterparty dispute history, no anti-farming trip, no impaired sole evidence). Your statement that you were at the marked bay and the rider did not appear is consistent with the trace, but a rider's absence does not make a short wait chargeable. No clause produces a referral, and no profile field was used as a ground against either party.",
    "amount_sgd_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

